### Goal Model Design for Food Delivery and Dirty Dish Retrieval in a Hospital Setting

The goal model is structured to ensure efficient food delivery and dirty dish retrieval, considering both autonomous and cooperative operations in a hospital environment.

#### Goals Overview

| Goal ID | Goal Title | Text | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation |
|--------|------------|------|-------------------|-----------|----------|
| G1     | Deliver Food | Ensure food is delivered to the correct room. | - | Achieve | - |
| G1.1   | Direct Delivery | Robot places food on the table. | ; | Perform | G1 |
| G1.1.1 | Navigate to Room | Move to patient's room. | - | Perform | G1.1 |
| G1.1.2 | Place Food | Deposit meal on table. | - | Perform | G1.1 |
| G1.2   | Tray Retrieval | Patient or helper fetches food from tray. | ; | Perform | G1 |
| G1.2.1 | Check Retrieval Ability | Determine if patient can retrieve. | - | Query | G1.2 |
| G1.2.2 | Assist Retrieval | Provide assistance if needed. | ; | Achieve | G1.2 |
| G2     | Retrieve Dishes | Collect dirty dishes from the room. | - | Achieve | - |
| G2.1   | Autonomous Retrieval | Robot collects dishes alone. | ; | Perform | G2 |
| G2.1.1 | Navigate to Room | Move to patient's room. | - | Perform | G2.1 |
| G2.1.2 | Collect Dishes | Gather dirty dishes. | - | Perform | G2.1 |
| G2.2   | Assisted Retrieval | Retrieve with help. | ; | Perform | G2 |
| G2.2.1 | Check Assistance Need | Assess if help is required. | - | Query | G2.2 |
| G2.2.2 | Obtain Assistance | Secure helper for retrieval. | - | Achieve | G2.2 |

#### Justifications

- **G1**: The primary goal is to ensure food delivery, decomposed into two OR options for flexibility.
- **G1.1**: Sequential actions ensure the robot navigates and places food correctly.
- **G1.2**: Checks ability before assistance, ensuring correct meal retrieval.
- **G2**: Ensures dirty dishes are retrieved, with options for autonomous or assisted methods.

#### Tasks Overview

| Task ID | Task Title | Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots | Justification |
|---------|------------|------|----------|----------|------------------|---------------|
| AT1.1   | Navigate Room | Move to patient's room. | AND | Hospital | 1 | Single robot for accuracy. |
| AT1.2   | Place Meal | Deposit on table. | AND | Patient Room | 1 | Precision required. |
| AT1.3   | Fetch Food | Retrieve from tray. | AND | Patient Room | [1,2] | Cooperation possible. |
| AT2.1   | Check Ability | Determine patient's ability. | AND | Hospital | 1 | Centralized check. |
| AT2.2   | Assist Meal | Help retrieve meal. | AND | Patient Room | 1 | Direct assistance. |

### Summary

The goal model is designed to handle both food delivery and dish retrieval efficiently, considering various scenarios of patient ability and availability of assistance. Each goal is decomposed into actionable tasks, ensuring the system can adapt to different situations while maintaining efficiency and correctness.
